\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% TRANSFORMATION TauxGLUEclPtc
< m1:I1::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
           [ mu1,
             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                       [ I2:mu2,
                         auxrel/I3::VERB{VERBrec1}[mu7],
                         cliticrel/CLITIC{}[I5:mu4],
                         head/I4::VERB{VERBrec2}[mu3],
                         mu6
                       ],
             mu5
           ]
>

< m:I1::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
           [ mu1,
             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                       [ I2:mu2,
                         auxrel/I3::VERB{VERBrec1}[mu7],
                         gluerel/GLUE{},
                         cliticrel/CLITIC{}[I5:mu4], 
                         head/I4::VERB{VERBrec2}[mu3],
                         mu6
                       ],
             mu5
           ]
>


   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: (SENTENCErec1.finiteness = Infinite) AND
           ((SENTENCErec1.VRcompl = false AND
             SENTENCErec1.restructuring = false)  OR
            (SENTENCErec1.restructuring = true  AND
             SENTENCErec1.VRcompl = true))
       I2: NOT EXIST(mu2, [cliticrel/..])
       I3: VERBrec1.modo IN [Infinitivo, gerundio]
       I4: VERBrec2.modo = PtcPas
       I5: EXIST (mu4, [I51:rel1/..])
                 I51:rel1 IN [seCLrel, unoCLrel, dosCLrel, tresCLrel]
      >


      COMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1:  @
         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1:  @
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TauxGLUEclPtc
\item[* relevant examples:] haber dicho lo $\rightarrow$ haber + GLUE + lo dicho
\item[* language:] Spanish
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] CLAUSEtoSENTENCE
\item[* class:] TC\_gluerules
\item[* date of creation:] 11-OCT-1988 15:05:51  
\item[* author:] Elly van Munster
\item[* copied from:] T2clGLUEinf
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 14/11/88\ \ \ \ \ author: Elly van Munster\\
Test on VRcompl added.
\item date: 11/01/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo
\item date: 31/10/90\ \ \ \ \ author: Elena Pinillos
The clitic has been already moved before this rule applies; this rule
creates just a GLUE between the infinitive and the clitic
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To move the CLITIC-node to the right of the infinite 
aux (haber) and to create a GLUE in between: \\
haber dicho  CLITIC{} $\rightarrow$
haber + GLUE + CLITIC{} dicho
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
